WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.020
A 63,701 vote BJP lead in Assam opens counting that test Bengal and Tamil Nadu. This is Omni View Asia Pacific, episode 17. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Counting started Friday for five assembly by-poles in Tamil Nadu, West Bengal and Puducheri, plus Assam's Nagoun seat in the Lok Sabha. The Hindu reports BJP candidate Devasi Sharma is ahead of AIUDF's Mohamed Badrdeen Ajmal there,

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.940
and Congress candidate Sibamoni-Bora is third.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.840
In Tamil Nadu's Dharapuram seat, reserved for scheduled casts,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.620
the ninth round had TVK's P. Sathyabama on 24,047.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.320
AIA DMK's K. Bonamathi had 21,935.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.340
DMK's S. Suganya, 19,972.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.580
NAM Tamalar Kachis M. Karthika, 1,891.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.920
And the CPI's P. Lakshmanon, 442.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:02.120
In Pudicherry's Thatton Chavity, ruling AINRC candidate Ashok Anand kept a clear lead

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.200
over the Congress and DMK candidates, and party workers started celebrating.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.580
West Bengal's Nondegraham and Rijanagar count began at 8 in the morning under tight security.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:18.440
The BJP took office in May with 207 of 294 seats, so these by-poles will not chain two

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:18.980
governs.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:24.980
Tuesday's turnout was 80.89% in Nondegraham and 80.08% in Rijanagar.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:31.960
The Election Commission called the polling more or less peaceful, opposition parties alleged intimidation and demanded a fresh poll.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:40.000
The BJP rejected that. Across the region, a Sydney currency trader has won an unfair dismissal case after working offshore without permission.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:49.280
The Guardian reports the Fair Work Commission ruled on Wednesday that HIFX Australia, trading as XE, unfairly dismissed Charles Graham last December.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.820
He had also been in Bali while telling his manager he was at home.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:58.280
home. The Commission awarded no compensation. In Vietnam, a Melbourne anti-trafficking activist

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:03.380
is being held on terror charges. The Sydney Morning Harold reports. Australia's consulate

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.780
is seeking access. His family says the charges are fabricated.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:13.020
Also today, police in Chattasgar say four CRPF personnel were hurt on Thursday evening. Two

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.740
of them seriously, when a fragment exploded during disposal of leftover explosives near

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.440
the Alarmadgu camp in Sukhima.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.640
In many porous calmjong, Assam rifles in Indian Army teams neutralized 27 improvised bombs

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.460
along 8 kilometers of the Shaankeloak Pilong route.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.140
Days after four tankal Naga civilians were killed near Pilong.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.200
Pacific Scoop reports drought has been declared in parts of Tonga, as El Nino intensifies.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.480
And the Taipei Times reports the ministry has confirmed United States presence at Taiwan's

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.600
Hanquang exercises.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.020
In the wider world, New Zealand's censor said Friday it cannot block a planned, live-streamed

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.640
execution in the United States.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.800
The person is a former Army major.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.300
Rights groups want governments to protest that decision in Washington.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:01.280
On the case on both sides, Seoul is arguing over whether National Security Advisor

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.020
Y-Sung-Lak should go to Washington.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.660
Yeon-Ha reports the National Intelligence Service said Thursday it was kept out of a

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.360
June meeting with the United States and Japan on North Korean cyber threats.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.720
A news report said Washington requested that exclusion.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.800
The agency played the snub down.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.480
A senior ruling block insider told YonHap that several problems have already shaken

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.300
the relationship, and that trouble in the intelligence channel is never desirable.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.460
Some want the presidential office to send why to comment.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.980
The earlier break, as YonHap describes it, came after unification minister ChangDongYong

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.880
disclosed a uranium enrichment site in KooSong in March.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.040
Chang said he had only repeated what was already public.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.220
Washington then limited some of Seoul's access to North Korea intelligence.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.100
Against a trip now, a ruling block official says there appear to be no plans to send

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.440
why, though other options should be looked at.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.160
The industry ministry separately dismissed a report that U.S. Commerce Secretary Howard

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.500
Lutnik distressed the spy agency during investment talks.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.320
Everyone in that argument accepts the same point.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.520
The NIS was not in the June meeting.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:06.360
No travel date has been set.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.260
The ruling Democratic Party says a U.S. visa for former leader representative Jong-Chung

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:16.200
Ray is still under review, with no decision after he planned an audit of Seoul's missions

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:16.500
there.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.580
spokesperson Park Sung-Joon wants both governments to clear that fast.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.440
A sign of progress is new money pledged to Pacific climate resilience.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:30.120
The post-currier reports form Secretary-General Baron Divevesi-Walka welcomed commitments

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.620
that now total $190 million U.S. dollars for the Pacific resilience facility.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:40.600
Fiji put in $10 million, announced by Prime Minister Situveni Rabuka at the Pacific Preseop

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.120
in Nadi.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.120
Denmark added $2.3 million and the Netherlands $1 million, $13.3 million in this round.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:52.320
The first target is $500 million, and the longer aim is $1.5 billion.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.860
Waka called it Pacific Lead, with Pacific priorities in ownership and charge.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.580
Leaders restated that priority at their September meeting in Palau.

